FP16 instructions obeyed MXCSR.DAZ and MXCSR.FTZ

AVX512-FP16 spec, chapter 4: FP16 operands are neither conditionally
treated as zero (MXCSR.DAZ) nor flushed to zero (MXCSR.FTZ). Conversions
from FP32/FP64 still obey DAZ for their source; conversions producing
FP32/FP64 still obey FTZ. The AVX10.2 VMINMAXPH/SH pseudocode says the
same with daz=false.

Every AVX512-FP16 handler built its softfloat status with
mxcsr_to_softfloat_status_word(MXCSR), and the f16 softfloat routines honour
both bits, so with DAZ or FTZ set nearly every FP16 instruction changed its
result or its MXCSR flags: vaddph 2^-24 + 2^-24 gave 0 instead of 2^-23,
vmulph 2^-14 * 0.5 gave 0 instead of 2^-15, vminmaxph lost denormals, the
FP16 -> integer conversions dropped PE, vfpclassph classed a denormal as
zero, and so on across arithmetic, FMA, complex, compare/comi, fpclass,
getexp/getmant/reduce/rndscale/scalef, sqrt/rcp/rsqrt, min/max/minmax and
the conversions.

Fixed at the handlers, not in softfloat: AMX-FP8 converts through
f16_to_f32 and relies on its DAZ.
- sse_pfp.cc: new mxcsr_to_softfloat_status_word_fp16() with DAZ and FTZ
  cleared.
- cpu_templates_pfp.h: the FP16-only {k}-masked *_HALF templates use it;
  new unmasked HANDLE_AVX_PFP_{1,2,3}OP_HALF twins of the shared templates,
  declared in cpu.h and used by the 27 unmasked AVX512-FP16 entries in
  decoder/ia_opcodes_evex.def.
- avx512_pfp16.cc, the FP16 scalar FMA macros (avx512_fma.cc, avx_fma.cc),
  vrcpph/sh, vminmaxph/sh and vcomxsh use it; vrsqrtph/sh and
  vfpclassph/sh no longer read MXCSR.DAZ.
- avx512_cvt16.cc: FP16 -> anything and integer -> FP16 use it; the
  FP32/FP64/integer -> FP16 conversions keep MXCSR.DAZ and clear FTZ only,
  as avx_cvt.cc already does for F16C VCVTPS2PH.

Found 2026-09-29 by running all 297 FP16/BF16/FP8 opcode entries under
MXCSR 1F80, 1FC0 and 9F80 and comparing results and flags: afterwards only
the FP32/FP64-source conversions differ, and only under DAZ.

